1
00:00:00,494 --> 00:00:03,994
(Zack:)It sounds easy, but there's a lot of science
that goes into designing them.

2
00:00:10,296 --> 00:00:13,216
(Howard:)Happy now? I'm moving the dirty sock.

3
00:00:15,218 --> 00:00:16,848
(Sheldon:)Thank you.

4
00:00:17,178 --> 00:00:19,678
(Sheldon:)Raj, keep an eye out for the other one.

5
00:00:20,681 --> 00:00:23,021
(Penny:)-Hey, guys. This is my friend Zack.
ZACK: Hey.

6
00:00:23,184 --> 00:00:27,184
(Sheldon:)-Hello.
-Whoa, is that the laser? It's bitchen.

7
00:00:28,189 --> 00:00:30,689
(Sheldon:)Yes. In 1917...

8
00:00:30,858 --> 00:00:34,448
(Sheldon:)...when Albert Einstein established
the theoretic foundation for the laser...

9
00:00:34,612 --> 00:00:36,952
(Sheldon:)...in his paper
Zur Quantentheorie der Strahlung...

10
00:00:37,114 --> 00:00:41,664
(Sheldon:)...his fondest hope was that
the resultant device be "bitchen."

11
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:44,250
(Zack:)Well, mission accomplished.

12
00:00:47,208 --> 00:00:48,998
(Leonard:)Let me explain what we're doing here.

13
00:00:49,168 --> 00:00:51,548
(Leonard:)In 1969, the astronauts on Apollo 11...

14
00:00:51,712 --> 00:00:53,502
...positioned reflectors on the moon.

15
00:00:53,673 --> 00:00:55,713
We're gonna shoot a laser
off one of them...

16
00:00:55,883 --> 00:00:58,553
(Leonard:)...and let the light bounce back
into this photomultiplier.

17
00:00:58,719 --> 00:01:00,299
Oh, that's very cool.

